# One owner for everything, so `require_code_owner_review` on the main
# ruleset resolves to a person — it was set before this file existed and
# enforced nothing until 2026-09-18.
#
# Review requests route here automatically. The ruleset's admin bypass still
# applies, so the owner's own merges are not gated on this.
* @moneymikeMD

# Deliberately UNOWNED (a pattern with no owner). Dependabot's action-version
# bumps touch only these files, and a bot can neither be a code owner nor
# satisfy a code-owner review, so owning this path would make the
# patch/minor auto-merge policy inert.
#
# The tradeoff, stated plainly because it cuts the wrong way: workflow files
# are the highest-blast-radius thing in this repo, and this exempts exactly
# them from the code-owner gate. They are NOT ungated — the ruleset still
# requires one approving review and a green `selftests` check on every PR,
# and only patch/minor bumps auto-merge; a major still waits for a human.
/.github/workflows/

# Same exemption, same reason: the docs site's dependency manifest and
# lockfile. Dependabot updates these two files and nothing else when it bumps
# an Astro or Starlight version, so owning them would put the patch/minor
# auto-merge policy behind a review only a human can give.
#
# Scope is deliberately the two files, not the directory: everything else
# under docs/preview/website/ is site CONTENT and stays owned.
/docs/preview/website/package.json
/docs/preview/website/bun.lock
